// Rule: [T1547.001] Chosen Brick - Spaced Windows Run Key
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1547.001
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceRegistryEvents
// Purpose: Hunts for a Run-key value pointing to C: \Windows \SysWOW64, the actor-created lookalike directory most commonly observed for CHOSEN BRICK payload staging.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceRegistryEvents for spaced windows run key using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceRegistryEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: A match indicates the source-observed persistence artifact; it does not prove CHOSEN BRICK execution, Telegram C2, collection, or exfiltration.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// CHOSEN BRICK - Run-key persistence to a non-standard spaced Windows directory
// Status: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceRegistryEvents
// Source-observed behavior: HKCU Run-key persistence and the most commonly
// observed payload directory C:\Windows \SysWOW64 (literal space after Windows).
// A match indicates the source-observed persistence artifact; it does not prove
// CHOSEN BRICK execution, Telegram C2, collection, or exfiltration.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith @"\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run"
| where RegistryValueData contains @"C:\Windows \SysWOW64\"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, ActionType,
          RegistryKey, RegistryValueName, RegistryValueData,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessAccountName, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
